  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Southern Border’s righteous path forces meet over Fang Yuan’s coming tribulation. Wu Yong argues that Shadow Sect’s headquarters are in Southern Border and that Fang Yuan is likely to undergo tribulation there. A Tie clan Gu Immortal proposes building Beacon Towers, and Wu Yong supports it. Ba clan’s first supreme elder supports Wu Yong, asking what Southern Border has when Central Continent has Heavenly Court and Northern Plains has Longevity Heaven, and agrees to those Beacon Towers. Chi clan’s first supreme elder Chi Qu You expresses support, then Luo clan, Hou clan, and Chai clan express a strong intent to unite. The immortals treat this as historically new: not a superficial proclamation, but true close cooperation. Wu Yong names the union the Southern Alliance and sets Fang Yuan as its first target, then the other four regions.",
      "chapters": [
        1620
      ],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "righteous-path-union",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_southern_border",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "char_wu_yong",
        "fac_shadow_sect",
        "fac_tie_clan",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "fac_ba_clan",
        "reg_central_continent",
        "fac_heavenly_court",
        "reg_northern_plains",
        "fac_longevity_heaven",
        "fac_chi_clan",
        "char_chi_qu_you",
        "fac_luo_clan",
        "fac_hou_clan",
        "fac_chai_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The alliance leader’s position is empty, and Wu Yong is the number one choice for it. Other rank eight Gu Immortals withhold aid while Fang Yuan targets Wu Yong, because they do not know how he would treat the other clans if he took the seat.",
      "chapters": [
        1626
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "leader-seat",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Southern Alliance obtained Tao Zhu’s true inheritance. After Lu Wei Yin rescued many Southern Border rank seven Gu Immortals from Fang Yuan’s hands, he represented Paradise Earth’s force and officially joined the Southern Alliance.",
      "chapters": [
        1680
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "alliance-gains",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "inh_tao_zhu_true_inheritance",
        "char_lu_wei_yin",
        "char_paradise_earth_immortal_venerable"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Wu Yong appears in Central Continent with many Southern Alliance Gu Immortals and calls them to destroy Infallible blessed land. They answer that they will follow him as Alliance Leader.",
      "chapters": [
        1705
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
